WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.973
What you see on the screen are called 4’o clock plants:

00:00:07.973 --> 00:00:10.120
the plants that bloom with flowers

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:13.050
usually in the evenings!

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:16.644
We know they are used for decorative purposes,

00:00:16.644 --> 00:00:20.160
but can you think of any other uses for them?

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.560
These plants have immense importance in the

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:26.320
field of cytology and genetics!

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.660
These plants were first used by the German

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:31.580
botanist Carl Correns for his cytological

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:32.960
and genetic studies.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:36.800
They were used to explain an interesting concept

00:00:36.806 --> 00:00:38.969
of Cytoplasmic inheritance.

00:00:38.969 --> 00:00:43.280
Also, these plants are used by many geneticists

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:46.480
to study incomplete dominance!

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.180
What does this mean?

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:51.000
So far, we have studied only “Dominance”

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.600
of characters in the pea plant.

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:55.840
What does this concept of “Incomplete Dominance”

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:56.540
mean?

00:00:56.980 --> 00:01:01.239
Let us begin with understanding the name!

00:01:01.239 --> 00:01:03.800
Incomplete here means partial.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:06.560
Does it indicate that the dominance is partial?

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.530
That’s right!

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:11.640
The dominant character expresses itself, but

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:13.340
not completely.

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:15.654
It means that the dominant alleles do not

00:01:15.654 --> 00:01:18.080
completely mask the effect of the recessive

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:19.860
alleles.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:22.400
As a result, offsprings with intermediate

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.020
characters are obtained.

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:27.686
This is the reason why the phenomenon is also

00:01:27.686 --> 00:01:31.100
called “Partial Dominance” or “Semi-dominance”.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.080
Let us get back to our 4 o’clock plants

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:35.840
to understand this!

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:39.500
In this case, if a cross of homozygous red

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:42.500
and white flowered plants is carried out,

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:46.100
then the resultant offsprings are pink in colour.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:50.329
So the blend of red and white gives us a pink colour!

00:01:50.329 --> 00:01:53.106
This is because the dominant allele for the

00:01:53.106 --> 00:01:55.689
trait “red” does not completely mask the

00:01:55.689 --> 00:01:58.080
effect of the recessive allele for the trait

00:01:58.080 --> 00:01:59.000
“white”.

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:02.640
So when the alleles are expressed in the offsprings,

00:02:02.656 --> 00:02:05.090
they give an effect which is like a blend

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:06.939
of both!

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:10.030
This is the reason why we get pink flowers!

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:13.820
The same feature is seen in a snapdragon flower.

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:17.843
A red variety crossed with a white variety

00:02:17.843 --> 00:02:19.950
gives us pink flowers!

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:22.600
However, this is not a complete exception

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:23.760
to Mendelism.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:27.540
If the pink flowers are crossed, then the

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.900
F2 generation gives us the typical 1 to 2

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:33.000
to 1 genotypic ratio!

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:35.400
How does this happen?

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:38.800
Let us assume “RR” in capital to be the

00:02:38.808 --> 00:02:40.680
genes for Red flower colour.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:44.119
Let “ww” in lower case be the genes for

00:02:44.119 --> 00:02:46.500
representing white flowers.

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.740
On crossing the two, we get all the pink flowers

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:52.340
with the genotype “Rw”.

00:02:52.349 --> 00:02:55.285
Now till this step, we find the inheritance

00:02:55.285 --> 00:02:57.470
to be an exception to Mendelism.

00:02:57.470 --> 00:03:00.570
That’s because Mendelian genetics did not

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:03.140
talk about blending of characters!

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:07.798
However, on crossing any two from the F1 generation,

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:11.400
we obtain the genotypic ratio of 1 to 2 to

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:14.100
1 in the F two generation.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:17.580
Even though the phenotypic ratio is not ‘3

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:20.560
to 1’, the genotypic ratio obtained is the

00:03:20.569 --> 00:03:23.190
same as we had obtained earlier!

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:27.115
So this pattern of inheritance seen in snapdragon

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:30.620
is an exception to Mendelism, but not entirely.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:34.798
Because the F2 generation still exhibits the

00:03:34.798 --> 00:03:37.470
genotypic ratio ‘1 to 2 to 1’!

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:41.577
And if you noticed well, this is the phenotypic

00:03:41.577 --> 00:03:42.800
ratio as well!

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:47.510
Now this was about incomplete dominance in plants.

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:49.810
Is this seen in animals as well?

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:53.420
Oh yes, it is seen in human beings too!

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:56.637
Out of the many characters that show this

00:03:56.637 --> 00:04:00.010
kind of pattern, hair type is the one which

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:04.159
exhibits the pattern of incomplete dominance!

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:06.300
Curly and straight are the two types of hair

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.640
traits which we know.

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:10.920
Crossing these types gives us the third phenotype

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:12.240
which is wavy hair.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:15.660
This is nothing but an example of incomplete

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:16.580
dominance.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:19.900
Let us try out the theoretical cross now.

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:23.224
Let us assume “CC” in capital to be the

00:04:23.224 --> 00:04:25.270
genotype for curly hair.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:28.985
Similarly, let “ss” in lower case be the

00:04:28.985 --> 00:04:31.400
genotype of straight hair.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:35.246
Here, the trait of curly hair type is dominant

00:04:35.246 --> 00:04:39.509
over the trait of straight hair which is recessive.

00:04:39.509 --> 00:04:42.540
Can you solve this cross further to find the

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:45.680
genotypic ratio in the F two generation?

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:49.030
This is what we get on solving this further!

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:52.726
The F1 generation will all have Wavy hair;

00:04:52.726 --> 00:04:56.510
that is a blend of curly and straight hair.

00:04:56.510 --> 00:05:00.060
So all the offsprings here will have “C

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:03.060
s” as the genotype and Wavy hair as the

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:04.060
phenotype.

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:08.000
And the F2 generation will be obtained in

00:05:08.001 --> 00:05:11.310
the ratio ‘1 to 2 to 1’, both phenotypic

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:14.259
as well as genotypic!

00:05:14.259 --> 00:05:17.089
This is how incomplete dominance is found

00:05:17.089 --> 00:05:19.780
not only in plants but even in animals.

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:23.460
But how does it help us?

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:26.085
When it comes to plants, we obtain several

00:05:26.085 --> 00:05:28.710
beautiful phenotypes which can be used for

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:31.160
many purposes!

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:33.580
Animals exhibiting incomplete dominance are

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:36.580
excellent models for genetic studies.

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:41.199
Are there other types of exceptions to Mendelism?

00:05:41.199 --> 00:05:42.600
Yes!

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:45.120
There is one more in the list!

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:48.080
Let us have a look at it in the next part!

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:53.640
Zeki visited his uncle’s poultry farm where

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:57.980
he was amazed to see a variety of fowls around!

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:02.360
However, what caught his attention was this rooster!

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:03.889
Why?

00:06:03.889 --> 00:06:07.130
Notice that it has both: black and white feathers.

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:11.030
Zeki was curious to know about this fowl.

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:13.735
His uncle explained that such kind of chicken

00:06:13.735 --> 00:06:16.380
are commonly obtained when a black feathered

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:18.979
and a white feathered chicken are bred!

00:06:18.979 --> 00:06:21.300
But this is a simple account.

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:24.511
It does not explain the reason for this chicken

00:06:24.511 --> 00:06:27.790
to have checkered pattern or speckling feathers!

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:31.639
Any idea how this pattern of feathers is obtained?

00:06:31.639 --> 00:06:35.840
Let us understand it with the help of Genetics!

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:36.910
Yes!

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:39.255
The logical and correct explanation of this

00:06:39.255 --> 00:06:41.490
pattern is given by the phenomenon called

00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:44.770
“CODOMINANCE” in genetics.

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:47.550
This is another type of exception to Mendelism.

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:51.210
The term “Codominance” can be divided

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:54.870
into two parts, “CO” and “Dominance”.

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:57.400
We know what “co” stands for.

00:06:57.400 --> 00:07:00.080
It means mutual or together.

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:03.293
Just like “co-operation” which means operating

00:07:03.293 --> 00:07:04.690
or working together!

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:08.170
The second part is dominance.

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:10.120
And we know what dominance means!

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:13.104
An allele that masks the effect of the other

00:07:13.104 --> 00:07:16.020
recessive allele is said to be the dominant

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:16.960
one.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:20.020
This gives rise to a dominant phenotype!

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:23.620
Now the question is: how do the two terms

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:26.220
“CO” and “Dominance” come together

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:27.500
to give us the effect?

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:31.040
And what type of effect is exactly seen in

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:32.660
the organisms?

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:35.264
“Codominance” is the phenomenon where

00:07:35.264 --> 00:07:38.360
both the dominant alleles are equally strong

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:42.569
and thus expressed in the offspring simultaneously.

00:07:42.569 --> 00:07:45.534
So the offspring will be heterozygous and

00:07:45.534 --> 00:07:48.860
will have both dominant genes in the genotype.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:51.800
As a result, the effect of both the alleles

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:55.580
will be seen in the organism phenotypically.

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:57.540
How do you think we got this chicken with

00:07:57.540 --> 00:07:59.440
checkered feathers?

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:02.460
In such a case, we cross a black feathered

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:05.420
chicken with a white feathered one.

00:08:05.430 --> 00:08:08.301
To understand this theoretically, let us say

00:08:08.301 --> 00:08:10.780
that we have the genes “BB” in capital

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:14.165
for black coloured feathers and “WW” in

00:08:14.165 --> 00:08:17.290
capital for white coloured feathers.

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:20.352
On crossing the two, we get a progeny with

00:08:20.352 --> 00:08:22.320
all heterozygous genotypes.

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:27.140
Each offspring has one “B” and one “W” allele.

00:08:27.140 --> 00:08:29.780
That means each chicken has both the dominant

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:30.800
alleles.

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:33.615
And both the dominant alleles try to express

00:08:33.615 --> 00:08:34.219
themselves.

00:08:34.219 --> 00:08:37.974
As a result, we get both the characters expressed

00:08:37.974 --> 00:08:40.810
in all the offsprings phenotypically.

00:08:40.810 --> 00:08:44.020
Thus, all the chicken have checkered or in

00:08:44.020 --> 00:08:47.280
other words speckling feathers!

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:49.680
Now this is like an exception to Mendelism,

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:50.960
but not totally!

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:54.920
Just like incomplete dominance, even Codominance

00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:57.200
follows a pattern.

00:08:57.200 --> 00:09:00.820
The F2 generation is obtained in the typical

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:03.920
genotypic ratio 1 to 2 to 1.

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:06.940
And the offsprings in the F2 generation exhibit

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:10.680
the same ratio phenotypically as well!

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:14.820
We get 1 black, 2 speckled and 1 white offspring

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:17.200
in the F2 generation.

00:09:17.209 --> 00:09:19.180
This is the phenotype.

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:21.830
And what about the genotype?

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:25.239
We get one offspring with the genotype “BB”,

00:09:25.239 --> 00:09:28.339
two with “BW” and the last with genotype

00:09:28.339 --> 00:09:29.720
“WW”.

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:33.268
This is how Codominance is seen in the chicken

00:09:33.268 --> 00:09:36.970
which gives us a completely different phenotype.

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:39.738
Codominance is observed in humans as well

00:09:39.738 --> 00:09:41.899
when it comes to Blood grouping!

00:09:41.899 --> 00:09:44.350
Let us understand this in detail.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:50.130
How many blood group types do we have by the way?

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:52.680
There are many types actually, but we mostly

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:56.620
take into consideration the ABO type.

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:59.870
And this type divides has how many groups?

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:03.470
There are basically 4 groups according to this system.

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:07.550
These are A, B, O and AB group.

00:10:07.550 --> 00:10:11.920
Let’s say this is a single red blood cell.

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:14.340
There are various components attached to its

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:17.560
surface which are called antigens.

00:10:17.570 --> 00:10:21.450
These can be long chains of proteins or sugars.

00:10:21.450 --> 00:10:23.698
Now in case of the blood grouping system,

00:10:23.698 --> 00:10:26.000
the different groups are classified on the

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:28.630
basis of these antigens.

00:10:28.630 --> 00:10:31.987
So if the RBC has an “A” antigen, then

00:10:31.987 --> 00:10:34.019
the blood group is “A”.

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:37.460
Similarly, presence of “B” antigen categorises

00:10:37.460 --> 00:10:38.940
the blood as “B”.

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:43.650
In case of “O”, there are no antigens present at all!

00:10:43.650 --> 00:10:46.839
And now can you guess which antigen will be

00:10:46.839 --> 00:10:49.880
present on the RBCs if the group is “AB”?

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:51.480
That’s right!

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:54.960
The RBCs will have both the antigens “A”

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:58.200
and “B” present on their surfaces.

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:01.340
Getting back to our concept, how is Codominance

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:04.000
seen in these blood groups?

00:11:04.010 --> 00:11:06.244
In the case of human blood groups, the types

00:11:06.244 --> 00:11:09.520
“A” and “B” are both dominant, while

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:11.280
“O” is the recessive type.

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:15.011
Now if the offspring has one allele for “A”

00:11:15.011 --> 00:11:17.579
blood group and the other for “B” blood

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:20.100
group, then the phenotype obtained will be

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:22.160
“AB” blood group.

00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:25.074
This is how Codominance is found in humans

00:11:25.074 --> 00:11:27.010
in the case of blood groups.

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:30.960
Apart from humans, there are several other

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:34.680
animals that exhibit Codominance.

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:38.530
Cattle for example have roan coat colour.

00:11:38.530 --> 00:11:41.000
This is obtained on crossing cattle having

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:43.470
white coat colour with cattle having a red

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:46.180
coat colour.

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:48.960
Many other animals have a skincoat with two

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:52.280
colors, or have patches on their skin coat,

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:55.440
which are examples of codominance.

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:58.479
But note that not all animals with patches

00:11:58.479 --> 00:12:01.300
will always be examples of Codominance!

